On Wednesday 28 April 2004 15:07 Jakob Creutzig
(creutzig@mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de) wrote:

> First, keep one wish for emergency situations.
> (You can wish for a cockatrice corpse, e.g..)
> Second, if you are so well-equipped, you might
> consider running wishless.  

I'm currently trying a wishless W; looking forward to making my own
DSM :-)

> The thing you need 
> most urgently is a gentle weapon, but it is
> maybe better to sacrifice for it than to wish
> for it.  

I beg to differ: the +2 Magicbane is perfectly adequate for a wizard who
has attack spells at 0% and is high enough level to do lots of damage
with magic missiles. Of the five or so Ws I ascended, three never
wielded anything else once they had it; the first was before weapon
skills, the remaining one lost the Magicbane in a BoH accident and was
reduced to wielding Vorpal Blade.

If Thoth (or Anhur as the case may be) does give you a long sword, train
up to Basic in it by all means. It doesn't hurt to have the skill, and
you can be Skilled or Expert in all magic skills you want and still
have the slots to spare.

> A ring of free action is very useful 
> for much later, but you will stumble over some
> dozen rings until then, hence you shouldn't
> wish for it right now.  

Unless you're having trouble with being paralyzed and beaten up. (I do
sometimes wish for it at the Castle if I have almost everything else).

> A helm of brilliance 
> raises your Int and Wis by one point for each
> point of enchantment, regardless of restrictions.
> However, this is by no means necessary for
> ascension.  

If all your failure percentages, or at least those you care about, are
at 0% you don't need a helm of brilliance at all. If you can cast magic
missile and cure sickness at 0% you don't really need a helm of
brilliance; those are the really indispensable spells.

> Some nicer spellbooks are always 
> good (finger of death etc), but again you might
> find or polypile them.  

Identify, magic mapping. But since you have a bag full of blank paper,
you might try writing them; Ws have a good chance of success in writing
unknown spellbooks. And you'll get a spellbook of finger of death if
you're crowned. (Praying for spellbooks is also possible, but
unreliable, and as you've got the Magicbane you must have a coaligned
altar to make it easier)

Some means of levitation.

Magic markers, and more magic markers.

